  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "The models now read the organisation, Patient and Practitioner keys the rebuilt mart sends.\n\t\t  - A full re-probe of the mart at production scale found 80 clinical keys being sent that no model property read. These were dropped silently on the way in. This release binds 58 of them.\n\t\t  - Thirteen models now carry the organisation identifier triple: AuthorOrganisationId, ProviderOrganisationId and RecordOwnerOrganisationId. Each model gets exactly the ids its own variant sends.\n\t\t  - Patient now carries PersonId, RegistrationType, RegisteredGpName, GpPracticeCode, HomePhone, UsualGpPractitionerId and GenderSourceConceptId.\n\t\t  - Practitioner now carries PersonId, PractitionerInRoleId, OrganisationId, Role, RoleCode and the latest episode of care details.\n\t\t  - PractitionerInRole now carries PersonId, the episode of care details and the managing organisation id, code and name.\n\t\t  - No FHIR output changes. These properties make the data available to the mappers; nothing in the bundle moves.\n\t\t  Dependencies moved on in this release: Hl7.Fhir.STU3 to 6.8.0, Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection to 10.0.14 and Microsoft.Extensions.Logging to 10.0.14.",
